{
  "version": 8,
  "name": "WhereWild Standard VersaTiles (Light)",
  "metadata": {
    "ww:note": "Recolor of WhereWild's own OpenMapTiles-schema standard-light.json layer structure using VersaTiles' real published 'Colorful' palette (github.com/versatiles-org/versatiles-style, src/styles/colorful.ts) \u2014 code + visual design both Unlicense/public domain (LICENSE.md in that repo), no attribution required. VersaTiles' own style JSON targets their own 'Shortbread' tile schema (source-layer names like 'earth'/'roads'/'buildings'), incompatible with our planetiler-built OpenMapTiles-schema PMTiles, so this ports their actual named color values (land/water/wood/grass/park/etc.) onto our existing layer structure rather than their layer definitions directly. The dark variant is generated algorithmically from the light palette via VersaTiles' own invertLuminosity() transform (HSL, hue/saturation unchanged, lightness L -> 100-L \u2014 see src/color/hsl.ts) rather than hand-designed, mirroring how VersaTiles derives their own 'Eclipse' theme from 'Colorful'."
  },
  "glyphs": "{fontstack}/{range}.pbf",
